From a2683dddd3d0af64ad62bbb44fb4899a8b6b7bb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:41:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/54] hw/display/pvg: loops, private memory, LLVM intrinsics;
 blits, samplers, continuations, mip layouts

air2spv: natural loops with OpLoopMerge, dedicated continue blocks and
split loop headers so inner selections merge inside the loop; selection
merges clamped into the innermost loop; alloca as Function-storage word
arrays with offset-tracked pointers; LLVM intrinsics (fmuladd, fma, fabs,
min/maxnum, ...); forced inlining of helpers; 32-bit derivatives of half
values. All 141 captured guest shaders now pass spirv-val (vulkan1.3).

pvg-exec: blit segments executed on guest memory (buffer<->texture,
texture->texture, buffer->buffer, fill); Metal sampler objects decoded
into VkSamplers; continuation render segments resume the previous pass;
texture objects with several mip levels; skipped-pass and written-range
diagnostics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
